Of nouls' 475 catalogue questions, 105 (22%) are about a family a deterministic zanity rule detects, so zanity answers them without a model, and zanity `--infer` asks 327 (69%) itself, as rules named for their family. The other 43 are about families only C, C++, PHP or Perl can have, which zanity has no grammar for.

# Asking the same model

Each named question asked about a fixture written to have the problem it asks about, by both tools, of the same model, kev-4b, served locally. The probability is how sure the model was that the problem is there; a finding needs 0.8. Settled: a deterministic zanity rule found it, so zanity didn't need to ask. Both reported 3 of 28.

